      <text:p text:style-name="Body">OpenLintel • Educational planning resource • September 26, 2026</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">Illustrative teaching extension of The Window Room; not a client record, supplier quote, site survey, or construction-ready document. Pending professional review.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="RustHeading">How to use</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Body">Adapt the outline to the services you actually offer. The example is a fictional teaching document with no quoted fee, real client, or enforceable terms. It is not a contract and does not replace professional legal review of an agreement. Check every proposed output against your actual services; separate unpriced items, allowances, and exclusions.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•　Summarize discovery in the client’s language.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•　Pair each proposed deliverable with a clear phase and review.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•　Discuss assumptions and exclusions before preparing a separate agreement.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="ReviewHeading">Review before use</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•　Do not copy sample services into an offer you cannot deliver.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•　Do not mix design fees with the furniture purchasing budget.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Bullet">•　Do not present this educational proposal outline as a legal contract.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="FinalNote">Replace illustrative information with verified project records. No approval, legal agreement, or construction readiness is represented. Keep completed client documents in your own secure system.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="PageTwoStart">Your project</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Subhead">Project understanding</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Instruction">Restate the client’s intended outcome and identify the information you have relied on.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Entry">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Subhead">Proposed approach</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Instruction">Explain the sequence and where client decisions will be needed.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Entry">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Subhead">Proposed deliverables</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Instruction">Name each output and the level of development. Avoid an undefined promise of “all drawings”.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Entry">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Subhead">Phases and reviews</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Instruction">Describe review gates rather than inventing a universal project duration.</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="Entry">[Enter your project information here. Leave unknowns explicit.]</text:p>
